    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0294" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg288"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Mr. Merrill.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                        1889</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    telegram of the 2th instant, touching an attempt made on the 30th of July last,
                    to subvert the existing Government of the Hawaiian Islands and the landing of
                    men from the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Adams</hi> to protect lives and
                    property.</p>
                <p>I transmit for your files a copy<anchor n="*" xml:id="d107-f1"/> of the telegram
                    as deciphered and have to express the satisfaction of the Government that the
                    insurrection was suppressed with no greater losses than you report.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d107-f1" n="*" xml:id="d107-f1-content">
